.DS_Store
node_modules/

# Generated by `bun run fixtures`; a nested .git is an embedded repo git will not track.
tests/fixtures/

# This repo's own ledger and board are personal process, not part of the public repo.
# `.personal-config.json` is the same: one machine's archive path, which is what `setup`
# itself keeps out of a tracked repo (`src/render/repo.ts` `renderIgnore`).
/HANDOFF.md
/PASSOFF.md
/CLAUDE.local.md
/.personal-config.json

# But it *ships* files with those names, as templates and as worked examples. A global
# gitignore of `HANDOFF.md` (unanchored, so it matches at every depth) would otherwise make
# them invisible — which is exactly what happened on 2026-09-15. These re-include them.
!examples/HANDOFF.md
!examples/PASSOFF.md
!templates/HANDOFF.md
!templates/PASSOFF.md
!templates/CLAUDE.local.md
!templates/skills/handoff.md
!templates/skills/passoff.md

# The published bundle — built by `bun run build`, never committed.
dist/
